From: patrickdass93 <patrickdass93@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:13:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(gchat): resolve clarify prompts from card clicks,
 ack after the handler
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ce-type branch for card clicks logged "ack'd (v2 feature, deferred)" and
dropped the event: a clarify card's buttons rendered, but tapping one only
ended Google's loading bar. _handle_card_click now resolves the pending
prompt from the clicked button's clarify_id + choice via clarify_gateway
(mirroring the Slack adapter: "Other" flips to text-capture, an unknown or
expired id gets an honest expiry note) and patches the card in place.

Card clicks are acked only after the handler has run (_handle_click_bounded),
bounded well under the subscription's ackDeadline. Fire-and-forget submit plus
an immediate ack is at-most-once: a transient failure lost the click with no
redelivery. On a crash or a timeout the message is nacked for redelivery —
after cancelling the submitted task, so the original handler cannot keep
running alongside its redelivery — with a short backoff so a deterministic
failure cannot hot-loop the subscription. Both resolve paths are idempotent
under redelivery. _submit_on_loop gains a ``track`` flag so the awaited
caller, not the fire-and-forget logger, owns the failure report.

Card strings go through i18n (three new en keys next to the existing
google_chat clarify keys).
